course: dictionary
lesson: 3796
title: Forbid and its forms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When someone says you must not do something, they forbid it. «Running in the corridors is strictly forbidden» means you are not allowed to run there. Forbid means to say no, firmly, to something.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Signs that say «forbidden» warn you before you do something wrong. Rules at school and on beaches often forbid things to keep you safe, such as swimming without a lifeguard. Ask yourself: what is being stopped here? That is the clue.
explain: The word changes its shape. Forbids is for one person now, forbade is for the past, and forbidden is used with words like «is» or «strictly». To check your meaning, swap in «not allowed». «Some parks forbid picking flowers» becomes «Some parks do not allow picking flowers». It still makes sense, so you have got it.
fact: Forbid means to say that someone must not do something, or not to allow it.
fact: «Forbidden» means not allowed. «Strictly forbidden» means never allowed.
fact: You can write forbid someone to do something, or forbid someone from doing something: «The rules forbid us from climbing the fence.»
fact: «God forbid» is an old phrase that means I hope it never happens.
fact: One of the Ten Commandments forbids lying about others.
exercise: «Some parks and beaches forbid picking nature treasures.» What does forbid mean here? | *Not allow it | Help it along | Share it with everyone | Count it carefully
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means not allowed: «Swimming without a lifeguard is strictly forbidden.» | swimming | lifeguard | *forbidden | without
exercise: «Yesterday the teacher ___ us to run in the corridor.» Which word fits best? | *forbade | forbidding | forbids | forbidden
test: Mum says, «I forbid you to play on the road.» What does forbid mean? | Ask you nicely | *Say you must not do it | Let you do it | Help you find a game
test: Which phrase means I hope it never happens? | *God forbid | Forbid someone to | Forbidding light | Strictly forbidden
exam: Jayden says forbid means to help. Who is right? | Jayden, because forbid means help | Both, because forbid means lots of things | Only in parks | *Nobody, because forbid means to say something is not allowed
